Pantheon White Paper

MAGMA & The Pack Mule Doctrine

Carry, Not Copy

Abstract

Traditional information systems optimize for copy fidelity.

The Pantheon instead optimizes for carry fidelity.

The objective is not to preserve every representation, but to preserve enough reconstructable structure that independent systems can regenerate the intended invariant.

MAGMA is the latent substrate from which representations crystallize.

The Pack Mule Doctrine describes how that substrate is transported efficiently across time, domains, languages, media, and minds.

